Z||000000||swoods||09-07-2001||11:54 AM||||I have an 85 gt automatic and I have an 84 2m4 4 speed. And I was wondering how hard is it to convert  my 84 over to the gt. I would like to keep the 4 speed but I dont know if I can.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fiero_24||09-07-2001||12:18 PM||||Are you talking about just the motor and trans, the body, or all of the above?<P>Craig<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||swoods||09-07-2001||12:28 PM||||Im talking about the motor ,trany, bumbers, sunroof,and dash. I dont think Im going to be able to get a clear title on the Gt thats the only reason Im considering the swap.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||09-07-2001||01:04 PM||||The wiring may be a challange.  The 84 had no V6 option in mind, so the wiring harness after the engine into the body, the wires don't exactly match.  So no easy plug and play.  It can be done.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fiero_24||09-07-2001||02:18 PM||||As far as the body it will be easy.  I took an 85 Coupe V6 and turned it into a GT fastback (PICS ON MY SITE).  Just watch the A pillar when taking the sunroof off, plus the sunroof mounts (I think 7 or 8 of them) tend to strip out due to rust.  As far as the motor swap I am not sure.  <P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||84Bill||09-07-2001||10:05 PM||||If your talking body parts, not a problem. If your talking engine welp you got a heap of work but it can be done.||||reg||1
Z||000006||swoods||09-08-2001||01:23 AM||||Alright I know everything will have to be changed Ill pretty much have to gut the Gt to do this. My big concern is though the 84 is a 4 speed so does that mean Ill have to swicth the 84 to an auto matic or is there a way I can keep the 4 speed.If I cant keep the 4 speed than what all needs to be changed for me to make the 84 an automatic.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Leper||09-08-2001||02:22 AM||||You'll need to get a computer from a 4 speed trans v6 car.<BR>Swap the engine cradle, but keep the 4 speed.||||reg||1
Z||000008||jelly2m8||09-09-2001||06:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Leper:<BR><B>You'll need to get a computer from a 4 speed trans v6 car.<BR>Swap the engine cradle, but keep the 4 speed.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No You dont need a V6/ 4spd ECM. It is the same P/N for auto and standard shift. The only difference is the EPROM. The Auto EPROM in there will work fine with the std transaxle, No I can't tell what the difference is, but I run a auto EPROM in my V6 5 spd with no ill effects.<P> The EPROMS are available through GM for about 50 bux canuk If you do want to change it.||||reg||1
